(1060792, 54599, 19493, '<td valign="top">Hi David,<br/>This isn''t really stbrown3rd, this is his girlfriend, but I liked your photo.  It brought back memories of my college years spent surveying the oilshale lands outside of Vernal Utah.  Beautiful country.  I like to think that maybe one of my survey markers is atop that Ridge.  Great shot.</td>', 'Hi David,This isn''t really stbrown3rd, this is his girlfriend, but I liked your photo.  It brought back memories of my college years spent surveying the oilshale lands outside of Vernal Utah.  Beautiful country.  I like to think that maybe one of my survey markers is atop that Ridge.  Great shot.', '2004-12-13 20:41:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1143754, 54542, 31637, '<td valign="top">a 10 all the way. Beautiful background, perfect time to take this during rush hour because of the sky and the rich blue color.</td>', 'a 10 all the way. Beautiful background, perfect time to take this during rush hour because of the sky and the rich blue color.', '2005-02-01 01:00:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1146604, 54542, 32749, '<td valign="top">Great Shot, especially as I live in Lancing (the lights in the distance). I had a similar idea to take a shot from there. It''s good to know I am thinking like a great photographer.</td>', 'Great Shot, especially as I live in Lancing (the lights in the distance). I had a similar idea to take a shot from there. It''s good to know I am thinking like a great photographer.', '2005-02-02 11:18:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1362777, 54542, 23394, '<td valign="top"><b>re-visiting my faves...</b> <br/> <br/>this is another image that i immediately latched on to upon discovering the dpc galleries.  of course, i was taken by the iamge--it is killer!  but, what is more important to me is the lesson it offers in <i>looking for potential in the world around you.</i> <br/> <br/>by day, this shot would barely register as a boring postcard (well, maybe a bit above--the curve leads nicely to the wave-like horizon--if the skies offered something).  but instead of simply treating it like the 1000s and 1000s of others who pass this way, mark saw the potential in what the vista could offer with the proper lighting.  granted, he may have gotten lucky with the skies, but, all the same, he had a vision of what he could capture, and just look at the result!  stunning!<br/> <br/>this image is a great reminder that not only should you always be looking while you are out and about, but you should also be asking yourself, "how would that or that look with a different light?"  there is no limit as to what you may capture if you learn to slow down your eyes.<br/> <br/>thanks for a great lesson!</td>', 're-visiting my faves...  this is another image that i immediately latched on to upon discovering the dpc galleries.  of course, i was taken by the iamge--it is killer!  but, what is more important to me is the lesson it offers in looking for potential in the world around you.  by day, this shot would barely register as a boring postcard (well, maybe a bit above--the curve leads nicely to the wave-like horizon--if the skies offered something).  but instead of simply treating it like the 1000s and 1000s of others who pass this way, mark saw the potential in what the vista could offer with the proper lighting.  granted, he may have gotten lucky with the skies, but, all the same, he had a vision of what he could capture, and just look at the result!  stunning! this image is a great reminder that not only should you always be looking while you are out and about, but you should also be asking yourself, "how would that or that look with a different light?"  there is no limit as to what you may capture if you learn to slow down your eyes. thanks for a great lesson!', '2005-05-05 09:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1463283, 54599, 15711, '<td valign="top">Terrific. Just found this one.  The blue is so rich. Great photograph all the way around.</td>', 'Terrific. Just found this one.  The blue is so rich. Great photograph all the way around.', '2005-06-17 13:11:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1672596, 54561, 43621, '<td valign="top">I think this is a good shot.  It''s very difficult to capture a photo at night with a FinePix 3800!  Good job.</td>', 'I think this is a good shot.  It''s very difficult to capture a photo at night with a FinePix 3800!  Good job.', '2005-09-04 07:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1770279, 54599, 31637, '<td valign="top">so great. I think these photos of mountains at night are very rare, and when I see these they all make my jaw hit the keyboard. It seems as if the majority of ambient light is coming from the left. Is that where the moon was ? if so, maybe you could of included it in your shot.</td>', 'so great. I think these photos of mountains at night are very rare, and when I see these they all make my jaw hit the keyboard. It seems as if the majority of ambient light is coming from the left. Is that where the moon was ? if so, maybe you could of included it in your shot.', '2005-10-08 16:13:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1959444, 54599, 49273, '<td valign="top">What A great Picture Nice Job..</td>', 'What A great Picture Nice Job..', '2005-12-17 23:59:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2564021, 54599, 16912, '<td valign="top">comment from my <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=336521&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">1-4-0</a>  thread...<br/> <br/>This really is a WOW! shot David. Without knocking the shot I wonder what it would score in todays dpc climate? I feel as if I want to be sitting in a deckchair within the image, relaxing and viewing the scenery. Dare I pic fault with a shot scoring 8.296? There seem to be quite a lot of white specs in the foreground? and is that really a red star? Even though you used some noise reduction software the sky still seems a little noisey to me.<br/> <br/>The colours, composition and light are just awe inspiring :)</td>', 'comment from my 1-4-0  thread... This really is a WOW! shot David. Without knocking the shot I wonder what it would score in todays dpc climate? I feel as if I want to be sitting in a deckchair within the image, relaxing and viewing the scenery. Dare I pic fault with a shot scoring 8.296? There seem to be quite a lot of white specs in the foreground? and is that really a red star? Even though you used some noise reduction software the sky still seems a little noisey to me. The colours, composition and light are just awe inspiring :)', '2006-06-28 21:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3137706, 54614, 34659, '<td valign="top">WOW...  This is riveting!  Fantastically disturbing image.  Severely underrated.  Beautiful work.</td>', 'WOW...  This is riveting!  Fantastically disturbing image.  Severely underrated.  Beautiful work.', '2006-12-21 00:01:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4336560, 54613, 86974, '<td valign="top">Happy Holidays Pedro,<br/> <br/>  My name is Melissa Prien. I was one of the individuals who wrote a comment on your collage girl image. In return you wrote to me and asked me when I was going to enter an image so you could return the critique. I have been doing a lot of shooting as of late and was wondering if you would turn your professional eye on a few  of my images before I place them in a local Artist show. I am far from being a pro like yourself but I dont think I am all that bad so any thing you have to say about my images good or bad would be welcome.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your time.<br/> <br/>Melissamp99@yahoo.com</td>', 'Happy Holidays Pedro,   My name is Melissa Prien. I was one of the individuals who wrote a comment on your collage girl image. In return you wrote to me and asked me when I was going to enter an image so you could return the critique. I have been doing a lot of shooting as of late and was wondering if you would turn your professional eye on a few  of my images before I place them in a local Artist show. I am far from being a pro like yourself but I dont think I am all that bad so any thing you have to say about my images good or bad would be welcome. Thank you for your time. Melissamp99@yahoo.com', '2007-12-26 16:11:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4340041, 54599, 73452, '<td valign="top">what a fantastic shot, and great job at the colours, most photograph these  night shots and try to mess with this beautiful blue.  And its from Utah, where i live, so you get cookie points for that, haha.  Great job once again.</td>', 'what a fantastic shot, and great job at the colours, most photograph these  night shots and try to mess with this beautiful blue.  And its from Utah, where i live, so you get cookie points for that, haha.  Great job once again.', '2007-12-27 23:48:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7241838, 54639, 19944, '<td valign="top">You know, this really isn''t all that bad.  Before reading your notes, I had to stop and really look at it.  While I never figured out what it was, it still held my attention.  To me, if I photo makes me stop and really look, it has been successful.</td>', 'You know, this really isn''t all that bad.  Before reading your notes, I had to stop and really look at it.  While I never figured out what it was, it still held my attention.  To me, if I photo makes me stop and really look, it has been successful.', '2014-07-17 17:52:07.000000', NULL, 0);
